<title>THAILAND: United Communication unit invests in U.S. firm.</title>
<headline>United Communication unit invests in U.S. firm.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>UCOM International Co Ltd, a subsidiary of United Communication Industry Plc, said on Monday it had bought 1.5 million shares in U.S.-based Inter WAVE Communications International Ltd.</p>
<p>The company said the stake, which accounts for 7.6 percent of the total shares of the American firm, were worth 11.5 cents apiece.</p>
<p>United Communication closed at 118 baht per share on Friday, down 12 baht.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
